 - `test-print` — prints **one** test page on the chosen printer. This uses paper.
 - `run` — keeps printing approved orders. Leave it running. Ctrl+C stops it safely.
 
-The agent works on A4 paper only, because the order does not yet record a paper size.
-A printer with no A4 option will refuse every order, and the owner sees why.
+Each order carries the paper size the customer chose (A4, A3 or Letter). The agent selects it
+on Linux/CUPS when the printer lists that size. On Windows the agent cannot read or choose the
+tray size yet, so the server refuses A3 and Letter orders for any shop with a Windows computer before
+the customer is charged, and customers are shown only A4 there. The agent still refuses a non-A4 job it
+cannot print, as a second check. A printer that cannot do the chosen size refuses the order, and the
+owner sees why. Owners should switch off paper sizes the printer cannot print.
 
